# Keep the build context to the sources the Dockerfile actually copies, and
# keep every credential-shaped path out of it whether or not one exists today.
.git
.github
.worktrees
.claude
target
plugin/node_modules
plugin/dist
# `plugin/build.mjs` walks plugin/build/ recursively and concatenates every .js
# it finds, so a stale local tsc output in the context would silently inject
# dead modules into the bundle and break the reproducible digest the release
# evidence manifest records. It is generated inside the image; never shipped in.
plugin/build
# The dashboard ships as-is, minus the two directories that are not the
# dashboard: `dev/` is a mock server for local development and `test/` is its
# suite. Neither belongs in an image whose whole argument is that it contains
# only what the server serves. Excluding them here rather than naming each
# shipped file in the Dockerfile means a new stylesheet or script ships
# automatically while a second mock server never can.
dashboard/dev
dashboard/test
bench/results
docs
chart
scripts
*.log
**/.DS_Store
**/__pycache__
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/.npmrc
**/.ssh
**/*.agekey
**/*.key
**/*.pem
**/*.p12
**/*.pfx
**/id_rsa*
**/id_ed25519*
**/known_hosts*
**/*credential*
**/keys.txt
**/kubeconfig*
**/*.kubeconfig
